$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for amide coupling: To a 0°C solution of carboxylic
acid (1.0 eq or 2.0 eq) in DMF (0.15 M) was added EDC (1.2 eq or 2.4 eq)
followed by HOAt (1.2 eq or 2.4 eq). After 10 min, amine (1.0 eq) and NMM
(3.0 eq or 6.0 eq) were added. The resulting reaction mixture was allowed
to warm to room temperature overnight and then poured into a separatory
funnel containing EtOAc and sat. aq. NaHCO3. The aqueous layer was
extracted with EtOAc (3 x). The combined organic extracts were washed
with 1 N HCl, 10% LiCl and sat. NaCl and then dried over Na2SO4, filtered
and concentrated in vacuo. (S)-tert-Butyl
4-oxo-2-(((R)-1,2,3,4-tetrahydronaphthalen-1-yl)carbamoyl)pyrrolidine-1-carboxylate,
29. Following the general procedure for amide coupling,
(S)-1-(tertbutoxycarbonyl)-4-oxopyrrolidine-2-carboxylic acid (36, 4.60
g, 20.1 mmol) and (R)-1,2,3,4-tetrahydronaphthalen-1-amine (37, 2.95 g,
20.1 mmol) were converted to 29 (6.17 g, 100%) after purification using
flash column chromatography (gradient from 0 to 35% EtOAc/CH2Cl2). 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CD3OD, mixture of amide rotamers) δ 7.40-7.22 (m, 1H),
7.20-6.99 (m, 3H), 5.06 (br s, 1H), 4.70 (dd, J = 9.9, 2.4 Hz, 1H), 3.87
(s, 1H), 3.71-3.43 (m, 1H), 3.11-2.92 (m, 1H), 2.89-2.69 (m, 2H),
2.56-2.33 (m, 1H), 2.13-1.72 (m, 4H), 1.58-1.39 (m, 9H); MS(ESI+) m/z
359.2 (M + H)+.
